WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:06.490
I promised I'd show you
how I found Helen's lost family.

2
00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.570
It was through her first cousins.

3
00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:14.160
For years, we assumed Zacharias
was alone in the camp.

4
00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:18.010
Then I looked more closely
at the Buchenwald roster page.

5
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.840
Let me ask you, what do you see?

6
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.500
I noticed Zacharias Helman.
That's who I'm related to.

7
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.350
That's all I noticed.

8
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.610
Anything else?
Anyone see anything else?

9
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.020
[Audience] 57101.

10
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.360
Yes, that is his prisoner number.

11
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.350
Well, look, two lines below him.

12
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.460
Another Helman, Michal.
57103.

13
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.580
It has been hiding in plain sight
since 2019.

14
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.250
I was so focused on
my immediate family only,

15
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.420
I never looked
for the same surname.

16
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.220
People were deported
with family and neighbors.

17
00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.730
So follow them too.

18
00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.070
Not every record survived,
as Jude mentioned as well.

19
00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.530
And sometimes following extended
family members or neighbors

20
00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.060
will lead you to your next record,
or the next place that person was.

21
00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:14.530
So I searched Michal's prisoner number,
57103,

22
00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:19.100
in the Arolsen Archives, and it ended up
being Zacharias's nephew.

23
00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.560
I didn't know at first.

24
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.720
He had a photo too.

25
00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:27.450
He was from the same village,
lived a few houses away,

26
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.740
and had the same trade as Zacharias.
Same job.

27
00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.750
Then, a couple weeks later,

28
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:41.790
I decided to go through all 1,000 people
on that transport list to Buchenwald.

29
00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.900
And on page six, a different page,
I found Lajos Helman,

30
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.080
prisoner number 56906,

31
00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.300
almost 200 numbers earlier,
Michal's older brother,

32
00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.640
with a photo too.

33
00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.300
Now there's three of them.

34
00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:06.760
Three family members, photographed
back to back to back on June 2nd, 1944,

35
00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.660
at Buchenwald, together again.

36
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:14.250
A Fuhrmann, or in Yiddish, a balagula:
a wagon driver.

37
00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.920
I kept seeing this trade, this job,
on record after record.

38
00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:24.250
It's a trade that's almost gone now,
and it became my connection to the past.

39
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:29.550
A wheel brings many spokes to one center,
the way this research brings

40
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.380
scattered records back to one family.

41
00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:37.280
That's why my logo is a wagon wheel,
12 spokes for the 12 tribes.

42
00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:42.250
Following each of these men's cards
through the camp,

43
00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.720
I found out that while my
great-grandfather Zacharias was murdered,

44
00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.840
the brothers, Michal and Lajos, survived.

45
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:55.950
Another older brother of Michal and Lajos,
Yaakov, had escaped before the war.

46
00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:01.080
And in 1997, from his kibbutz in Israel,
he filled out a Page of Testimony

47
00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.380
and put it on Yad Vashem for his parents
and his other murdered brothers.

48
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.550
I read them, and this year I contacted
the kibbutz's archives

49
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.520
and was put in touch
with their descendants.

50
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:18.000
Now we talk on WhatsApp, me in Hawaiʻi,
and most of them in Israel.

51
00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.950
Their children were never told
about Zacharias

52
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.550
or any of Helen's side
of the family.

53
00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:26.880
Maybe that much loss
was too hard to share.

54
00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.600
We will never know.

55
00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.850
So even if you think
you already know everything,

56
00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:35.200
there might be
something else to find.
